                <pb facs="0582" n="472" sameAs="frus:frus1931v03/pg472"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/2739: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-11-18T11:00:00+08:00">November 18, 1931—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received November 18—5:15 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>955. By mandate of National Government issued yesterday General Wan Fu-lin’s
                    resignation as Chairman of Heilungkiang is accepted and General Ma Chan-shan is
                    appointed in his stead.</p>
                <closer>For the Minister:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                        >Engert</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
